01:01:12.832 --> 01:01:15.239
I'm like, you gotta Heimlich maneuver me.

01:01:15.239 --> 01:01:16.072
It was awful.

01:01:16.072 --> 01:01:20.040
I spat out the boba in
the store. It was so bad.

01:01:20.040 --> 01:01:22.000
I suck on it, and like
the whitest thing ever,

01:01:22.000 --> 01:01:25.001
I went (coughing).

01:01:25.001 --> 01:01:27.401
- That is the whitest story ever.

01:01:27.401 --> 01:01:29.920
White man tries tapioca
for the first time.

01:01:29.920 --> 01:01:30.831
- Literally spat it out.

01:01:30.831 --> 01:01:32.395
And I was like, "I'm so sorry."

01:01:32.395 --> 01:01:34.154
He's like, "No, it was funny."

01:01:34.154 --> 01:01:35.737
And I'm like, "Oh, okay."

01:01:35.737 --> 01:01:38.725
I'm like, "But the milk part tasted good.

01:01:38.725 --> 01:01:39.985
Can we get rid of the balls?"

01:01:39.985 --> 01:01:41.535
And he's like, "Yeah, we'll
just make you another one

01:01:41.535 --> 01:01:42.368
without the balls."

01:01:42.368 --> 01:01:43.225
"No, no, no, you don't have to."

01:01:43.225 --> 01:01:44.175
He's like, "It's free, don't worry."

01:01:44.175 --> 01:01:45.815
I'm like, oh, okay.

01:01:45.815 --> 01:01:46.648
- I got you, bro.

01:01:46.648 --> 01:01:48.132
- I was like, "Aw, okay, okay, okay."

01:01:48.132 --> 01:01:48.965
- That's nice of him.

01:01:48.965 --> 01:01:49.798
- Yeah, he's very, very nice.

01:01:49.798 --> 01:01:51.815
- God, I remember when
the fucking initial boba

01:01:51.815 --> 01:01:53.174
explosion happened in Japan.

01:01:53.174 --> 01:01:54.614
- How did that happen?
Why did that happen?

01:01:54.614 --> 01:01:57.318
- That's so weird, 'cause
the month we moved here,

01:01:57.318 --> 01:01:59.363
it was like every boba store,

01:01:59.363 --> 01:02:01.101
you would tell which boba store,

01:02:01.101 --> 01:02:02.920
what was a boba store, sorry,

01:02:02.920 --> 01:02:03.780
if it had a line outside.

01:02:03.780 --> 01:02:04.739
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, right.

01:02:04.739 --> 01:02:06.412
- There were some boba stores
near my house at the time

01:02:06.412 --> 01:02:08.831
where it was like, legit, on weekends,

01:02:08.831 --> 01:02:11.084
it was legit like a four-hour wait.

01:02:11.084 --> 01:02:12.872
- Yeah, I don't get it.
- And I'm like, what?

01:02:12.872 --> 01:02:14.140
- I don't get it.

01:02:14.140 --> 01:02:16.260
It's just bit a tea with some jelly.

01:02:16.260 --> 01:02:17.812
- Man, did that die though.

01:02:17.812 --> 01:02:18.851
- Oh, yeah.

01:02:18.851 --> 01:02:20.323
- It fucking sped-run death.

01:02:20.323 --> 01:02:21.931
- Dude, I like-

01:02:21.931 --> 01:02:22.764
- Did it speed-run death?

01:02:22.764 --> 01:02:24.152
I think it's still-
- Oh, yeah.

01:02:24.152 --> 01:02:25.190
- No, you never see lines anymore.

01:02:25.190 --> 01:02:26.393
- No, you go to a boba store now.

01:02:26.393 --> 01:02:28.376
There's maybe one or two people there max.

01:02:28.376 --> 01:02:29.539
- That's true, that's true.

01:02:29.539 --> 01:02:31.959
Well, they're still a thing
in the UK from what I can see.

01:02:31.959 --> 01:02:33.501
They still exist, the stores still exist-

01:02:33.501 --> 01:02:35.896
- No, no, it's still around,
but it's not the hype.

01:02:35.896 --> 01:02:36.776
The hype is nowhere near.
- It's just the hype,

01:02:36.776 --> 01:02:38.008
but I mean, rightly so.

01:02:38.008 --> 01:02:40.008
'Cause I thought it
was overrated the fuck.

01:02:40.008 --> 01:02:40.977
- [Joey] I think so too.

01:02:40.977 --> 01:02:42.658
- I didn't get what the
craze around it was.

01:02:42.658 --> 01:02:45.112
- I mean, I drank a
shitload of it during uni,

01:02:45.112 --> 01:02:48.654
because we had a boba store
near where we studied.

01:02:48.654 --> 01:02:49.487
- [Connor] I get it.

01:02:49.487 --> 01:02:50.974
- Yeah, but that was before the explosion.

01:02:50.974 --> 01:02:53.641
- It lasts a while, 'cause it's cold.

01:02:53.641 --> 01:02:55.991
You can kinda just sip
on it throughout the day

01:02:55.991 --> 01:02:57.452
if you ever get a big one.

01:02:57.452 --> 01:03:00.274
- Also, if you're a uni student,
it's a great sugar rush.

01:03:00.274 --> 01:03:01.482
And also, it keeps you concentrated.

01:03:01.482 --> 01:03:04.374
- I guess, everyone after a
while was, in Japan at least,

01:03:04.374 --> 01:03:06.187
were like, all right,
back to Starbucks now.

01:03:06.187 --> 01:03:07.075
- [Joey] Yeah, back to Starbucks.

01:03:07.075 --> 01:03:10.005
- Back to the way life should've been.

01:03:10.005 --> 01:03:11.952
- I just saw nothing but just iced tea,

01:03:11.952 --> 01:03:14.613
or iced coffee, I don't know, maybe.

01:03:14.613 --> 01:03:16.378
To me, it was like-

01:03:16.378 --> 01:03:17.211
- But it's not fun.

01:03:17.211 --> 01:03:18.621
There's no personality.

01:03:18.621 --> 01:03:19.462
- I'm a hot boy.

01:03:19.462 --> 01:03:20.803
I like my drinks hot.

01:03:20.803 --> 01:03:22.587
I don't really like cold drinks that much.

01:03:22.587 --> 01:03:24.793
- They had hot boba too
though, right, I think?

01:03:24.793 --> 01:03:26.335
- Hot boba is just not the same.

01:03:26.335 --> 01:03:27.275
- They have hot boba?
- It's not the same.

01:03:27.275 --> 01:03:28.628
Yeah, I think they do.
- What?

01:03:28.628 --> 01:03:30.191
- But it's not as good.

01:03:30.191 --> 01:03:33.056
- I believe you can order
it with no ice sometimes.

01:03:33.056 --> 01:03:34.289
You know when you can
customize your order?

01:03:34.289 --> 01:03:35.477
- That's lukewarm though.

01:03:35.477 --> 01:03:36.490
- That is true, that's lukewarm.

01:03:36.490 --> 01:03:37.337
- That's like piss water.

01:03:37.337 --> 01:03:38.170
- [Joey] Warm boba?

01:03:38.170 --> 01:03:41.717
- Yeah, that's like pee water.
- Warm boba?

01:03:41.717 --> 01:03:42.579
- [Joey] Gross.

01:03:42.579 --> 01:03:45.070
- I don't know what maniac
would order a warm boba,

01:03:45.070 --> 01:03:46.300
but it was an option in some

01:03:46.300 --> 01:03:47.918
of the boba stores I've been to.

01:03:47.918 --> 01:03:50.952
- If it was a specialty, I'd
be like, okay, if you say so.

01:03:50.952 --> 01:03:52.527
- Was that a secret menu?

01:03:52.527 --> 01:03:54.052
- [Garnt] The secret menu!

01:03:54.052 --> 01:03:56.550
- Did you have to speak
Chinese to get that one?

01:03:56.550 --> 01:03:57.470
It's like, got my Chinese friend.

01:03:57.470 --> 01:03:59.201
Can I get the lukewarm boba?

01:03:59.201 --> 01:04:01.227
It's like, aw, you know your shit.

01:04:01.227 --> 01:04:02.881
- Yeah, I don't know.

01:04:02.881 --> 01:04:04.570
I don't know how or why it exploded,

01:04:04.570 --> 01:04:06.731
but I remember, not just in Japan,

01:04:06.731 --> 01:04:09.299
but just pretty much everywhere in the UK,

01:04:09.299 --> 01:04:12.325
everywhere in Thailand, you
just couldn't get away from it.

01:04:12.325 --> 01:04:13.875
- Even in the States,
I remember it was huge.

01:04:13.875 --> 01:04:14.897
- It was fashionable.

01:04:14.897 --> 01:04:16.644
I think it's just a fashionable drink.

01:04:16.644 --> 01:04:18.242
- Yeah, I guess so.

01:04:18.242 --> 01:04:19.342
- It's Instagram-able.

01:04:19.342 --> 01:04:20.175
That's it.
- Yeah.

01:04:20.175 --> 01:04:21.563
- It's Instagram-able.

01:04:21.563 --> 01:04:25.232
- Let's be honest, 2014
was all the Frappuccino.

01:04:25.232 --> 01:04:26.065
That's what it was.

01:04:26.065 --> 01:04:26.898
- That's true, that's true.
- It came out.

01:04:26.898 --> 01:04:27.731
That was the thing.

01:04:27.731 --> 01:04:29.838
Everyone just wants a photogenic drink,

01:04:29.838 --> 01:04:31.257
and boba looked photogenic.

01:04:31.257 --> 01:04:35.097
- But I feel Japan took
the photogenic-ness of boba

01:04:35.097 --> 01:04:37.158
and just was trying to stretch it out

01:04:37.158 --> 01:04:40.287
to such a high degree where
it was just so unnecessary-

01:04:40.287 --> 01:04:41.369
- That's like everything in Japan now.

01:04:41.369 --> 01:04:43.076
Everything is about taking photos.

01:04:43.076 --> 01:04:45.177
Afternoon tea, I love my afternoon tea.

01:04:45.177 --> 01:04:46.709
It's the most British
thing I've ever said.

01:04:46.709 --> 01:04:48.349
I really, really enjoy going for tea

01:04:48.349 --> 01:04:51.289
and having crumpets or scones.

01:04:51.289 --> 01:04:54.079
- That is a weirdly popular
subculture in Japan, isn't it?

01:04:54.079 --> 01:04:57.440
- It is, but everywhere I've
been just does it really badly.

01:04:57.440 --> 01:04:58.931
- [Joey] Really?

01:04:58.931 --> 01:05:00.459
- Okay, I mean, not
badly. It's hard to say.

01:05:00.459 --> 01:05:02.281
- [Joey] Not as good.

01:05:02.281 --> 01:05:04.266
- To me, afternoon tea is just as much

01:05:04.266 --> 01:05:06.495
about the food you get as it is the tea.

01:05:06.495 --> 01:05:07.328
- Yeah.
- Right.

01:05:07.328 --> 01:05:09.193
- And the food isn't great here.

01:05:09.193 --> 01:05:11.001
- The food here looks so aesthetic.

01:05:11.001 --> 01:05:11.883
- But it doesn't taste good.

01:05:11.883 --> 01:05:13.849
- Yeah, yeah, that's
literally all they do.

01:05:13.849 --> 01:05:14.761
They arrange it,

01:05:14.761 --> 01:05:17.042
and they get these
beautiful colored things.

01:05:17.042 --> 01:05:18.380
Then you take one bite of the quiche.

01:05:18.380 --> 01:05:21.000
You're like, why does it taste bad?

01:05:21.000 --> 01:05:22.985
- I actually agree.

01:05:22.985 --> 01:05:26.349
Afternoon is one thing
that England does the best

01:05:26.349 --> 01:05:27.414
that I've had so far,

01:05:27.414 --> 01:05:30.151
because the afternoon tea
food is actually good,

01:05:30.151 --> 01:05:32.792
whereas in Japan, every
time I've had afternoon tea,

01:05:32.792 --> 01:05:33.773
it just looks pretty.

01:05:33.773 --> 01:05:36.313
- Also, yeah, it's
gotta be layered, right?

01:05:36.313 --> 01:05:38.974
The layers are to distinguish
the types of flavors.

01:05:38.974 --> 01:05:40.632
Bottom is for sandwiches.

01:05:40.632 --> 01:05:42.690
Then maybe you get the quiches

01:05:42.690 --> 01:05:45.892
or the more savory kind of the dishes.

01:05:45.892 --> 01:05:46.725
It's always sandwich at the bottom.

01:05:46.725 --> 01:05:47.981
- Like pastries and stuff like that?

01:05:47.981 --> 01:05:49.458
- So it's savory.
- You got the sweets

01:05:49.458 --> 01:05:51.410
at the top.
- Savory, and then sweets.

01:05:51.410 --> 01:05:54.100
But in Japan, it's sweets, sweets,

01:05:54.100 --> 01:05:56.419
savory, and also sweets.

01:05:56.419 --> 01:05:58.279
It's ridiculous.

01:05:58.279 --> 01:06:00.320
'Cause normally, afternoon
tea, you kinda have it at,

01:06:00.320 --> 01:06:02.008
we'd have it in the afternoon.

01:06:02.008 --> 01:06:02.919
If it's a good place,

01:06:02.919 --> 01:06:05.067
you can normally skip
lunch or dinner with it,

01:06:05.067 --> 01:06:06.994
'cause it's quite a lot.

01:06:06.994 --> 01:06:08.864
Some places even refill.

01:06:08.864 --> 01:06:10.647
In the UK, they refill the sandwiches

01:06:10.647 --> 01:06:13.235
or stuff in some places.

01:06:13.235 --> 01:06:14.704
You can chow down.

01:06:14.704 --> 01:06:15.537
If you liked the sandwiches,

01:06:15.537 --> 01:06:17.528
or you liked whatever they're offering,

01:06:17.528 --> 01:06:18.898
dude, it's good, it's so good.

01:06:18.898 --> 01:06:20.027
You get your money's worth.

01:06:20.027 --> 01:06:21.217
Expensive though.

01:06:21.217 --> 01:06:22.326
In London, it's very expensive.

01:06:22.326 --> 01:06:23.159
- [Joey] Yeah, I bet.

01:06:23.159 --> 01:06:24.345
- It's good, it's really good.

01:06:24.345 --> 01:06:25.985
- But it's an experience
you're paying for, right?

01:06:25.985 --> 01:06:26.818
- [Garnt] Yeah.

01:06:26.818 --> 01:06:27.930
- Yeah, I get that.

01:06:27.930 --> 01:06:30.570
- One thing I've only seen
really in Asia as well,

01:06:30.570 --> 01:06:31.903
going off the boba thing,

01:06:31.903 --> 01:06:33.281
before, I guess, the boba craze took off-

01:06:33.281 --> 01:06:34.114
- It's the most privileged thing

01:06:34.114 --> 01:06:35.019
I've ever mentioned by the way.

01:06:35.019 --> 01:06:35.852
I just realized that.

01:06:35.852 --> 01:06:36.685
- What? Afternoon tea?
- I sound so privileged,

01:06:36.685 --> 01:06:39.227
me being like, "The tea isn't
good enough, disgusting."

01:06:39.227 --> 01:06:40.060
- [Joey] No sandwiches.

01:06:40.060 --> 01:06:41.845
- I mean, it's one thing I
feel like Britain does well,

01:06:41.845 --> 01:06:43.415
so I think it's a good-

01:06:43.415 --> 01:06:44.598
- It's no Greggs though, is it?

01:06:44.598 --> 01:06:45.431
- It's no Greggs.
- It's not Greggs.

01:06:45.431 --> 01:06:46.378
- It's not Greggs.

01:06:46.378 --> 01:06:50.393
But yeah, dessert cafes, that's one thing

01:06:50.393 --> 01:06:51.422
I only saw in Asia.
- Oh, god.

01:06:51.422 --> 01:06:52.437
- Oh, yeah.

01:06:52.437 --> 01:06:54.692
- I don't know if there is more
dessert cafes in the UK now-

01:06:54.692 --> 01:06:55.940
- Dessert buffets especially.

01:06:55.940 --> 01:06:57.909
- Sorry?
- Dessert buffets.

01:06:57.909 --> 01:06:59.076
- What's that?

01:07:00.319 --> 01:07:01.940
- It's literally exactly that.

01:07:01.940 --> 01:07:04.009
Think of a buffet, but it's all desserts.

01:07:04.009 --> 01:07:05.362
- Yeah, 'cause whenever I'd hang out

01:07:05.362 --> 01:07:08.040
with some of my friends in
Thailand, they'd be like,

01:07:08.040 --> 01:07:10.127
"Oh, let's go to this dessert cafe."

01:07:10.127 --> 01:07:11.469
I'm just like, wait.

01:07:11.469 --> 01:07:13.978
To me, growing up in England,
dessert was something you have

01:07:13.978 --> 01:07:16.427
at the end of the meal at a restaurant.

01:07:16.427 --> 01:07:20.796
You don't go to a specific
place to eat dessert, right?

01:07:20.796 --> 01:07:23.998
That concept was just alien to me.

01:07:23.998 --> 01:07:27.207
To me, it still feels weird, right?

01:07:27.207 --> 01:07:28.756
If I wanted dessert after a meal,

01:07:28.756 --> 01:07:30.472
I would order it at the restaurant.

01:07:30.472 --> 01:07:33.300
But you go to a dessert cafe,

01:07:33.300 --> 01:07:34.979
it's like half a meal, you know?

01:07:34.979 --> 01:07:36.198
- Yeah.

01:07:36.198 --> 01:07:38.301
- 'Cause you never go to a dessert cafe

01:07:38.301 --> 01:07:40.419
after you finish eating at a restaurant,

01:07:40.419 --> 01:07:41.778
but you go to a dessert cafe

01:07:41.778 --> 01:07:43.306
at really weird times at a day.

01:07:43.306 --> 01:07:44.391
- Three.

01:07:44.391 --> 01:07:45.900
- Yeah, three or something.

01:07:45.900 --> 01:07:47.659
I go to a dessert cafe,
I have the dessert,

01:07:47.659 --> 01:07:50.578
and then it just fucks
with my eating schedule.

01:07:50.578 --> 01:07:51.810
'Cause then I just don't want dinner,

01:07:51.810 --> 01:07:53.710
but then it also doesn't
fill me up as well.

01:07:53.710 --> 01:07:54.543
It's really weird.

01:07:54.543 --> 01:07:56.781
- So you get hungry at 9 PM.

01:07:56.781 --> 01:07:58.252
It's like a really weird
time where it's like,

01:07:58.252 --> 01:07:59.752
oh, it's kinda too late to eat food.

01:07:59.752 --> 01:08:01.315
- [Garnt] Yeah, right.

01:08:01.315 --> 01:08:02.993
- But I know I won't be able to sleep,

01:08:02.993 --> 01:08:04.341
'cause I'm gonna get hungry.

01:08:04.341 --> 01:08:05.174
- Yeah, yeah.

01:08:05.174 --> 01:08:06.863
- No, I get that.

01:08:06.863 --> 01:08:08.909
- I don't know, I just
don't feel satisfied

01:08:08.909 --> 01:08:10.682
if I've eaten a lot of something sweet.

01:08:10.682 --> 01:08:14.133
But when I eat a savory
meal, I just feel happy.

01:08:14.133 --> 01:08:16.962
- I just feel sick if I eat
too much sweet stuff now.

01:08:16.962 --> 01:08:17.961
I was always like that though.

01:08:17.961 --> 01:08:19.039
I could never eat too...

01:08:19.039 --> 01:08:21.841
I like sweets, but I could
never eat too much of it,

01:08:21.841 --> 01:08:23.041
'cause then I'd just get...

01:08:23.041 --> 01:08:25.293
I'd be filled up, but then that feeling

01:08:25.293 --> 01:08:26.750
of being filled up by sweet shit,

01:08:26.750 --> 01:08:28.843
it just made me feel really ill,

01:08:28.843 --> 01:08:31.252
which just made me wanna
eat regular food anyway.

01:08:31.252 --> 01:08:34.732
- Man, I said this a year or two ago,

01:08:34.732 --> 01:08:38.760
but man, I still don't
like themed cafes in Japan,

01:08:38.760 --> 01:08:41.332
the collaboration cafes.

01:08:41.332 --> 01:08:42.301
The food-
- Because of the food?

01:08:42.301 --> 01:08:44.242
- The food and drink is a joke.

01:08:44.242 --> 01:08:45.075
- It looks good.

01:08:45.075 --> 01:08:46.224
- That's the thing.

01:08:46.224 --> 01:08:50.966
I hate the fact that we're
turning food impractical.

01:08:50.966 --> 01:08:52.442
Okay, wow, we put a little...

01:08:52.442 --> 01:08:54.483
I went to the Square Enix one.

01:08:54.483 --> 01:08:55.360
- Oh, yeah.

01:08:55.360 --> 01:08:56.889
- And then they made me a latte.

01:08:56.889 --> 01:08:59.448
And I was like, this
latte tastes really bad.

01:08:59.448 --> 01:09:02.474
But they put a Slime on it,
so I guess now it's worth $9.

01:09:02.474 --> 01:09:03.807
It's like, what?

01:09:05.224 --> 01:09:06.776
- I've been to so many themed cafes,

01:09:06.776 --> 01:09:08.239
'cause Aki loves going to them.

01:09:08.239 --> 01:09:09.290
- I know.

01:09:09.290 --> 01:09:10.298
- 'Cause she makes content out of it,

01:09:10.298 --> 01:09:12.509
so it's understandable.

01:09:12.509 --> 01:09:15.498
I think the only good one
where I would actually go back

01:09:15.498 --> 01:09:18.666
for the food is the Kirby Cafe.

01:09:18.666 --> 01:09:19.963
I know it's good-
- Lies.

01:09:19.963 --> 01:09:21.073
- Sus, sus.
- No, no.

01:09:21.073 --> 01:09:22.307
I know it's good because-

01:09:22.307 --> 01:09:23.523
- The biggest Kirby fan of all-

01:09:23.523 --> 01:09:24.356
- No, no, no, no, no, hear me out.

01:09:24.356 --> 01:09:25.861
- Says the Kirby Cafe-
- Hear me out.

01:09:25.861 --> 01:09:26.889
