01:18:33.587 --> 01:18:36.337
who seem to run the neighborhood.

01:18:36.337 --> 01:18:38.056
I don't know how this happened.

01:18:38.056 --> 01:18:39.597
I don't know why this happened.

01:18:39.597 --> 01:18:41.980
But you do one thing wrong,

01:18:41.980 --> 01:18:44.875
maybe you take a garbage
out just a bit too early.

01:18:44.875 --> 01:18:47.177
You see them, you see them eyeing you.

01:18:47.177 --> 01:18:48.647
You see them eyeing you, right?

01:18:48.647 --> 01:18:50.087
I can tell.

01:18:50.087 --> 01:18:53.119
Anytime me and Sydney come out,

01:18:53.119 --> 01:18:56.834
sometimes they're just gossiping together.

01:18:56.834 --> 01:18:59.782
You know when you can feel
someone gossiping about you,

01:18:59.782 --> 01:19:03.383
that's every time me and
Sydney go out of the house.

01:19:03.383 --> 01:19:04.753
They're always in the same corner.

01:19:04.753 --> 01:19:08.581
It's the same group of Japanese
grandmas, and I remember-

01:19:08.581 --> 01:19:09.872
- We should wait for them to say hi.

01:19:09.872 --> 01:19:11.089
- Yeah, yeah, you should-
- No, I do, I do.

01:19:11.089 --> 01:19:12.650
- For those people, what I've learned

01:19:12.650 --> 01:19:15.428
is that you just need
to be ignorantly happy

01:19:15.428 --> 01:19:16.908
and friendly towards them.

01:19:16.908 --> 01:19:17.966
And then they'll start to be like,

01:19:17.966 --> 01:19:19.918
oh, maybe they're actually all right.

01:19:19.918 --> 01:19:23.412
Maybe we'll take them off
the hit list, you know?

01:19:23.412 --> 01:19:25.584
- Okay, I feel like I've been put...

01:19:25.584 --> 01:19:26.513
I was friendly enough, right?

01:19:26.513 --> 01:19:27.863
- There's so much moist-

01:19:27.863 --> 01:19:29.853
- Sorry.
- Amount of speaking here.

01:19:29.853 --> 01:19:32.534
(Connor moaning)

01:19:32.534 --> 01:19:34.861
- I feel like I've been
put on a hit list now,

01:19:34.861 --> 01:19:39.213
because I did unfortunately
take the garbage out

01:19:39.213 --> 01:19:40.298
on the wrong day.

01:19:40.298 --> 01:19:41.142
One day, one day.

01:19:41.142 --> 01:19:43.313
- Being on a Japanese
hit list is just like,

01:19:43.313 --> 01:19:46.280
I'll give you, at worst, a
passive aggressive note one day.

01:19:46.280 --> 01:19:47.232
- Yeah, I got that.

01:19:47.232 --> 01:19:48.103
- Yeah, yeah.

01:19:48.103 --> 01:19:48.936
- Did you really?

01:19:48.936 --> 01:19:50.394
- Yeah, remember?

01:19:50.394 --> 01:19:53.374
In my old apartment, I got
that English-written note.

01:19:53.374 --> 01:19:54.904
- Yeah, that's the worst you'll get.

01:19:54.904 --> 01:19:55.946
- [Joey] Yeah, that's
the worst you'll get.

01:19:55.946 --> 01:19:56.840
- They say they'll kick you out,

01:19:56.840 --> 01:19:58.226
and they'll tell the housing company.

01:19:58.226 --> 01:19:59.437
- And then I need (speaking
in foreign language)

01:19:59.437 --> 01:20:01.833
reverse Uno card, and then they shut up.

01:20:01.833 --> 01:20:03.180
- The housing company's
not gonna kick you out.

01:20:03.180 --> 01:20:04.013
- No, of course not.

01:20:04.013 --> 01:20:05.310
- Unless you are actually taking the piss.

01:20:05.310 --> 01:20:08.001
But if you're just walking,

01:20:08.001 --> 01:20:10.163
the housing company's
not gonna give a fuck.

01:20:10.163 --> 01:20:11.722
- They'd be like, okay, granny.

01:20:11.722 --> 01:20:12.555
- They'd be like, all right.

01:20:12.555 --> 01:20:14.101
- Simmer down, come on now.

01:20:14.101 --> 01:20:18.530
- So yeah, one day, normally,
we take our garbage out

01:20:18.530 --> 01:20:21.679
either the night before or the morning of.

01:20:21.679 --> 01:20:25.039
I don't know what's custom
in Japanese neighborhoods.

01:20:25.039 --> 01:20:26.749
- It depends on your area.

01:20:26.749 --> 01:20:28.868
- Yeah, normally, it's like,
I think, the morning of,

01:20:28.868 --> 01:20:32.920
but I remember, I think, I
woke up slightly late that day.

01:20:32.920 --> 01:20:35.654
So how it worked in my place is that,

01:20:35.654 --> 01:20:37.248
the garbage is one day.

01:20:37.248 --> 01:20:40.445
And then the recyclables is the next day.

01:20:40.445 --> 01:20:41.551
- Yeah, I hated that.

01:20:41.551 --> 01:20:42.746
- I think that's most places.

01:20:42.746 --> 01:20:47.324
- Yeah, yeah, so I thought
I was just on the cusp

01:20:47.324 --> 01:20:51.535
of getting the recyclables
out on the right day,

01:20:51.535 --> 01:20:55.375
'cause it's garbage,
recyclables, then garbage again.

01:20:55.375 --> 01:20:57.104
So I thought I was just on the cusp.

01:20:57.104 --> 01:20:59.295
Maybe the garbage truck hadn't come yet.

01:20:59.295 --> 01:21:00.872
So I go out to the garbage spot,

01:21:00.872 --> 01:21:02.514
and I see some bags there.

01:21:02.514 --> 01:21:06.887
I was like, oh, great,
I still made it in time.

01:21:06.887 --> 01:21:10.318
And so I put the recyclables
out, went back in my house,

01:21:10.318 --> 01:21:13.172
and just continue about my day.

01:21:13.172 --> 01:21:14.585
I get a ring on my doorbell.

01:21:14.585 --> 01:21:15.418
- Oh no.

01:21:15.418 --> 01:21:16.671
- I get a ring on my doorbell.
- No way.

01:21:16.671 --> 01:21:19.677
- And I'm just like, oh, it
must be a delivery or something.

01:21:19.677 --> 01:21:21.001
- Yeah.

01:21:21.001 --> 01:21:24.608
- I open the door, and it's
three old Japanese grandmas-

01:21:24.608 --> 01:21:25.930
- Oh my god.
- Just staring at me.

01:21:25.930 --> 01:21:26.763
- Are you serious?

01:21:26.763 --> 01:21:28.171
- Yeah, I am serious.

01:21:28.171 --> 01:21:30.100
- [Joey] Oh my god!

01:21:30.100 --> 01:21:35.100
- And I see my bag of recyclables
right in front of my door.

01:21:36.010 --> 01:21:37.260
- [Joey] Right.

01:21:38.132 --> 01:21:41.849
- I mean, they nicely
enough explained to me

01:21:41.849 --> 01:21:43.994
that I had missed the time
and it was just the wrong day

01:21:43.994 --> 01:21:46.304
to bring out the recyclables,

01:21:46.304 --> 01:21:49.222
but it kinda felt like
some fucking loan sharks

01:21:49.222 --> 01:21:51.035
outside my door being like-

01:21:51.035 --> 01:21:53.251
- It'd be a shame if this
were to happen again.

01:21:53.251 --> 01:21:54.084
- Yeah, yeah.

01:21:54.084 --> 01:21:55.973
- It's like repo men.

01:21:55.973 --> 01:21:58.713
You do it again, we're taking everything.

01:21:58.713 --> 01:22:00.342
- They are basically the gangsters

01:22:00.342 --> 01:22:01.813
that run the neighborhood, you know?

01:22:01.813 --> 01:22:04.675
I felt like I just missed out on paying

01:22:04.675 --> 01:22:06.504
the protection money of the day.

01:22:06.504 --> 01:22:08.013
It's like, shame what would happen-

01:22:08.013 --> 01:22:09.811
- America has the Crips and the Bloods.

01:22:09.811 --> 01:22:10.882
We have the Grannies.

01:22:10.882 --> 01:22:13.075
(all laugh)

01:22:13.075 --> 01:22:15.275
Fear them, they control everything.

01:22:15.275 --> 01:22:17.893
- Yeah, they're the real...

01:22:17.893 --> 01:22:20.081
It's like the fucking Sopranos, right?

01:22:20.081 --> 01:22:22.001
It's the Japanese Sopranos, right?

01:22:22.001 --> 01:22:22.834
The old Japanese grandmas-

01:22:22.834 --> 01:22:24.297
- Did you take the recycling out today?

01:22:24.297 --> 01:22:28.075
- I heard some really
strict crazy grandmas

01:22:28.075 --> 01:22:30.743
can get pissed off when,
you know on cardboard boxes?

01:22:30.743 --> 01:22:31.594
- [Joey And Garnt] Yeah.

01:22:31.594 --> 01:22:33.076
- Like the Amazon labels and stuff,

01:22:33.076 --> 01:22:34.667
they get pissed off you
don't take those off.

01:22:34.667 --> 01:22:35.584
- Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:22:35.584 --> 01:22:37.467
- I've heard of some
grandmas that get like,

01:22:37.467 --> 01:22:38.949
they're like, how dare you.

01:22:38.949 --> 01:22:40.635
Even though it doesn't make a difference.

01:22:40.635 --> 01:22:42.036
- No, of course not.

01:22:42.036 --> 01:22:44.916
- This is why I love living
in an apartment building.

01:22:44.916 --> 01:22:46.869
I can just take it down whenever I want.

01:22:46.869 --> 01:22:48.828
No recycling day.

01:22:48.828 --> 01:22:49.957
No garbage day.

01:22:49.957 --> 01:22:52.115
It's like, whenever you
have garbage, take it down.

01:22:52.115 --> 01:22:54.371
Cardboard's the worst,
'cause when you're moving in,

01:22:54.371 --> 01:22:56.688
it literally is like cardboard city.

01:22:56.688 --> 01:22:58.944
And it's just stacks
upon stacks upon stack.

01:22:58.944 --> 01:23:00.365
I'm waiting for the day when you're like,

01:23:00.365 --> 01:23:01.706
well, what's that in the corner, Connor?

01:23:01.706 --> 01:23:03.584
Well, it's the wall of cardboard actually.

01:23:03.584 --> 01:23:06.269
It's one of the main
attractions of the apartment.

01:23:06.269 --> 01:23:07.477
I have so much cardboard, in fact,

01:23:07.477 --> 01:23:10.585
that I could probably house
everyone in the half of Japan.

01:23:10.585 --> 01:23:13.220
- Yeah, I mean, that's the thing where,

01:23:13.220 --> 01:23:16.420
I remember when I was
moving in, I felt like,

01:23:16.420 --> 01:23:19.730
if you missed the day of
the cardboard collection,

01:23:19.730 --> 01:23:22.483
then you were just fucked, right?

01:23:22.483 --> 01:23:23.682
- Yeah, but also you feel like,

01:23:23.682 --> 01:23:26.602
am I taking the piss
with this much cardboard?

01:23:26.602 --> 01:23:30.651
I have a two-meter-high
stack of cardboard.

01:23:30.651 --> 01:23:33.660
Am I taking up too much
cardboard? Is that allowed?

01:23:33.660 --> 01:23:36.002
What's the limit on how much
recycling I can recycle?

01:23:36.002 --> 01:23:40.611
- I remember the only time
I had a granny experience

01:23:40.611 --> 01:23:43.338
when I was moving into my
current place was when,

01:23:43.338 --> 01:23:45.081
it was like the first
week I was moving in,

01:23:45.081 --> 01:23:48.043
and it was like the
shitload of cardboard thing.

01:23:48.043 --> 01:23:49.392
And cardboard day comes around.

01:23:49.392 --> 01:23:51.142
I'm just like, finally, here we go.

01:23:51.142 --> 01:23:53.615
This is where the cleansing starts.

01:23:53.615 --> 01:23:55.940
So I take out way too much cardboard,

01:23:55.940 --> 01:23:57.734
probably fucking half
the Amazon rainforest

01:23:57.734 --> 01:23:59.153
worth of cardboard, right?

01:23:59.153 --> 01:24:01.280
- [Connor] Naturally.

01:24:01.280 --> 01:24:03.179
- And then, the next morning,

01:24:03.179 --> 01:24:06.330
I come out to leave for the office, right?

01:24:06.330 --> 01:24:08.516
And a grandma stops me.

01:24:08.516 --> 01:24:09.893
And I'm like, oh no.

01:24:09.893 --> 01:24:11.691
- Uh oh, uh oh.

01:24:11.691 --> 01:24:13.451
- And she points at the
mountain of cardboard,

01:24:13.451 --> 01:24:16.525
and she's like, "That's
all your cardboard, right?"

01:24:16.525 --> 01:24:19.032
And I was like, "I mean, not all of it."

01:24:19.032 --> 01:24:22.013
- Oh, come on, love,
it's like 90%. Fuck off.

01:24:22.013 --> 01:24:22.955
- Yeah, most of it.

01:24:22.955 --> 01:24:26.249
And she's like, "I think
that you're really causing

01:24:26.249 --> 01:24:28.272
the rubbish people a lot of trouble

01:24:28.272 --> 01:24:29.772
with that much cardboard."

01:24:29.772 --> 01:24:31.880
And then I just reverse
Uno card, and I'm like,

01:24:31.880 --> 01:24:33.357
"I moved in yesterday."

01:24:33.357 --> 01:24:35.857
Puts on sunglasses, walks off.

01:24:37.211 --> 01:24:39.600
But legit, she was just
like, "Oh, I'm sorry then.

01:24:39.600 --> 01:24:41.761
I'm sorry about that."

01:24:41.761 --> 01:24:42.594
But that felt good.

01:24:42.594 --> 01:24:43.963
That was the one time
where I trumped the granny.

01:24:43.963 --> 01:24:46.452
I was like, you don't control it!

01:24:46.452 --> 01:24:47.285
- Silence!

01:24:47.285 --> 01:24:48.540
- Silence, woman!

01:24:48.540 --> 01:24:49.373
- [Ashley] You can actually,

01:24:49.373 --> 01:24:51.135
some moving companies say call them up.

01:24:51.135 --> 01:24:52.090
- Yeah, and take the cardboard.

01:24:52.090 --> 01:24:54.375
- Yeah, yeah, I did that, but even they,

01:24:54.375 --> 01:24:56.056
I had so much cardboard
that the moving company

01:24:56.056 --> 01:24:58.889
could only take so much cardboard.

01:25:00.318 --> 01:25:01.915
'Cause I moved into a much bigger place,

01:25:01.915 --> 01:25:03.929
and I needed to buy all this new furniture

01:25:03.929 --> 01:25:06.131
to fill up the space.

01:25:06.131 --> 01:25:07.010
But it felt good.

01:25:07.010 --> 01:25:08.542
It felt good to reverse Uno card a granny.

01:25:08.542 --> 01:25:11.318
- Basically, they think
organized crime in Japan

01:25:11.318 --> 01:25:12.837
is the Yakuza, no.

01:25:12.837 --> 01:25:13.670
- [Joey] It's the grandmas.

01:25:13.670 --> 01:25:16.418
- It's the Japanese grannies
in your neighborhood.

01:25:16.418 --> 01:25:18.799
Watch out, make sure
you don't piss them off.

01:25:18.799 --> 01:25:20.329
Otherwise, you're gonna
be having a bad time.

01:25:20.329 --> 01:25:21.551
- I've been living here for 60 years.

01:25:21.551 --> 01:25:23.890
I know every nook and
cranny of these streets.

01:25:23.890 --> 01:25:27.430
- Literally the day after
they came, I came back home,

01:25:27.430 --> 01:25:29.679
and they had slid this in my letterbox,

01:25:29.679 --> 01:25:33.030
just the schedule of the
garbage for the week,

01:25:33.030 --> 01:25:34.392
and the garbage collection.
- No.

01:25:34.392 --> 01:25:36.365
- That's so passive aggressive.

01:25:36.365 --> 01:25:39.614
- I was just like, oh,
they're sending me a message.

01:25:39.614 --> 01:25:40.586
They're literally sending me a message.

01:25:40.586 --> 01:25:41.680
- You turn over the
note, and they're like,

01:25:41.680 --> 01:25:44.093
get this wrong again, you're dead.

01:25:44.093 --> 01:25:46.026
Don't fuck it up again, Garnt.

01:25:46.026 --> 01:25:50.443
- Gonna wake up in bed with
a decapitated horse head.

01:25:52.556 --> 01:25:55.546
Get the garbage day right
next time. Don't fuck up.

01:25:55.546 --> 01:25:57.413
- You'll have a dead
salmon at your front door.

01:25:57.413 --> 01:26:01.675
- It's like, you better take
this out on the right day.

01:26:01.675 --> 01:26:05.256
- What day does oily
containers go, Garnt? Hmm?

01:26:05.256 --> 01:26:06.606
- The ultimate test.
- A shampoo bottle?

01:26:06.606 --> 01:26:08.409
A shampoo bottle is not recycling, Garnt.

01:26:08.409 --> 01:26:09.912
- Oh my god.

01:26:09.912 --> 01:26:12.993
- I love it, you have
this spreadsheet of items

01:26:12.993 --> 01:26:15.994
that very specifically
cannot be recycled and stuff.

01:26:15.994 --> 01:26:17.124
- I have an app for it, dude.

01:26:17.124 --> 01:26:17.957
- [Connor] Oh my god.

01:26:17.957 --> 01:26:20.611
- Yeah, our ward created
an app being like,

01:26:20.611 --> 01:26:21.964
if you put in a certain item,

01:26:21.964 --> 01:26:24.025
it tells you exactly
what day to bring it out.

01:26:24.025 --> 01:26:25.731
- What sucks is that there's like,

01:26:25.731 --> 01:26:28.070
some items, you're like,
what the fuck is this?

01:26:28.070 --> 01:26:29.430
You know, like styrofoam, right?

01:26:29.430 --> 01:26:30.263
- [Joey] Yeah.

01:26:30.263 --> 01:26:32.542
- Have you had that packaging that's thin?

01:26:32.542 --> 01:26:34.040
It's like a paper styrofoam?

01:26:34.040 --> 01:26:34.942
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- Yeah.

01:26:34.942 --> 01:26:36.192
- What the fuck is this?

01:26:36.192 --> 01:26:37.292
Is this burnable?

01:26:37.292 --> 01:26:38.642
Is this paper, or is this-

01:26:38.642 --> 01:26:40.049
- Plastic?
- I don't know what this is.

01:26:40.049 --> 01:26:40.882
This is a mystery.

01:26:40.882 --> 01:26:43.056
And every time I ask anyone,
they're like, "I have no idea."

01:26:43.056 --> 01:26:46.452
I think it's burnable, but no one's 100%.

01:26:46.452 --> 01:26:47.693
Everyone's like, "Dude,
it's not gonna matter.

01:26:47.693 --> 01:26:48.825
Just put it in the burnable."

01:26:48.825 --> 01:26:49.685
- That's the thing.

01:26:49.685 --> 01:26:51.222
There's all these rules that are laid out

01:26:51.222 --> 01:26:52.822
that the grannies will enforce you on.

01:26:52.822 --> 01:26:55.136
But when you put it all into
a fucking bag and put it out.

01:26:55.136 --> 01:26:56.369
- [Garnt] Of course.

01:26:56.369 --> 01:26:57.799
- I heard that apparently the recycling,

01:26:57.799 --> 01:26:59.833
even though they make
you sort it very strict,

01:26:59.833 --> 01:27:01.448
that actually when it goes
to the plant apparently,

01:27:01.448 --> 01:27:04.368
I don't know how true this
is, that it's not actually,

01:27:04.368 --> 01:27:06.407
they don't recycle it as
well as you'd think they are.

01:27:06.407 --> 01:27:07.948
- Yeah.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:27:07.948 --> 01:27:09.381
- I would believe that.

01:27:09.381 --> 01:27:11.832
- I mean, fair enough.

01:27:11.832 --> 01:27:14.859
But fuck, dude, one time I went down

01:27:14.859 --> 01:27:17.442
to my recycling thing in my current place.

01:27:17.442 --> 01:27:18.692
I thought, hmm.

01:27:19.891 --> 01:27:21.429
I was putting out my
bottles in my bottle thing,

01:27:21.429 --> 01:27:24.920
and I noticed that there was 10-plus

01:27:24.920 --> 01:27:27.253
Bombay Sapphire gin bottles.

01:27:28.677 --> 01:27:33.677
And I was like, who has drank
this much Bombay Sapphire?

01:27:33.818 --> 01:27:35.295
This is a lot of gin.
- It wasn't you, right?

01:27:35.295 --> 01:27:36.403
- No, it wasn't me.

01:27:36.403 --> 01:27:37.236
I was gonna say-

01:27:37.236 --> 01:27:38.667
- I thought that was you.

01:27:38.667 --> 01:27:40.606
- As another person who
enjoys Bombay Sapphire gin,

01:27:40.606 --> 01:27:43.524
I was like, huh, I wonder who's
bought this much Bombay...

01:27:43.524 --> 01:27:44.962
I'm gonna keep saying
it, it's very satisfying.

01:27:44.962 --> 01:27:45.795
Bombay Sapphire gin.

01:27:45.795 --> 01:27:46.994
- Clearly, there's another
British person in your building.

01:27:46.994 --> 01:27:50.065
- I was like, either somebody's
running a bar secretly

01:27:50.065 --> 01:27:51.883
in their apartment that specializes

01:27:51.883 --> 01:27:53.595
in Bombay Sapphire cocktails.

01:27:53.595 --> 01:27:54.596
- Or someone had a good night.

01:27:54.596 --> 01:27:56.826
- Or there's a really
depressed British person

01:27:56.826 --> 01:27:58.283
somewhere in this apartment building

01:27:58.283 --> 01:28:02.105
who is really, really spending
a lot of money on gin.

01:28:02.105 --> 01:28:03.678
I just thought, why
would you have this many?

01:28:03.678 --> 01:28:05.312
They're all neatly stacked,

01:28:05.312 --> 01:28:08.644
almost like a Jenga-esque stacking style.

01:28:08.644 --> 01:28:10.865
This is definitely one
person who brought...

01:28:10.865 --> 01:28:12.255
I wonder, did they collect
them for a long time,

01:28:12.255 --> 01:28:13.653
and they thought, no, this is ridiculous.

01:28:13.653 --> 01:28:15.350
I can't collect this many bottles.

01:28:15.350 --> 01:28:16.716
'Cause some people will keep
their alcohol containers

01:28:16.716 --> 01:28:19.784
afterwards as a memory, but I guess,

01:28:19.784 --> 01:28:21.989
when you drink too much, you're
like, okay, this is just-

01:28:21.989 --> 01:28:23.880
- How many Bombay Sapphires is too many?

01:28:23.880 --> 01:28:25.128
- I just thought, I was
like, this is a lot.

01:28:25.128 --> 01:28:26.977
I'm like, what's going on here?

01:28:26.977 --> 01:28:29.160
I wonder, I was like, what a weird trash.

01:28:29.160 --> 01:28:31.058
You ever see peoples' trash,
and you think, what's going on?

01:28:31.058 --> 01:28:32.267
- Oh, yeah.
- What's going on with that?

01:28:32.267 --> 01:28:33.100
- Many times.

01:28:33.100 --> 01:28:35.528
I remember the weirdest one I saw was,

01:28:35.528 --> 01:28:39.159
it was a vacuum cleaner
that had been perfectly cut

01:28:39.159 --> 01:28:41.159
in half down the middle.

01:28:42.597 --> 01:28:45.736
I was like, how does that happen?

01:28:45.736 --> 01:28:48.019
- Someone's like, damn, man, I
just wanna see what's inside.

01:28:48.019 --> 01:28:49.468
- Yeah, it was a Dyson.

01:28:49.468 --> 01:28:50.690
It was the body of a Dyson,

01:28:50.690 --> 01:28:53.168
but it'd been perfectly
split down the middle.

01:28:53.168 --> 01:28:54.509
But there was only one half.

01:28:54.509 --> 01:28:56.142
And I'm like, where did the other half go?

01:28:56.142 --> 01:28:57.284
- Sounds like some serial killer shit.

01:28:57.284 --> 01:28:58.177
- It was just one half?

01:28:58.177 --> 01:29:00.873
- It was only one half.

01:29:00.873 --> 01:29:03.468
For five minutes, I was
kinda looking around seeing.

01:29:03.468 --> 01:29:04.617
I wonder where the other half is.

01:29:04.617 --> 01:29:06.106
I couldn't find it.

01:29:06.106 --> 01:29:08.097
So he's either kept the other half,

01:29:08.097 --> 01:29:10.907
or I've witnessed some crucial evidence

01:29:10.907 --> 01:29:12.672
of a crime scene or something.

01:29:12.672 --> 01:29:13.925
I don't know what.
- That's so specific.

01:29:13.925 --> 01:29:15.196
- It was the weirdest thing.

01:29:15.196 --> 01:29:16.153
At least, I was like,

01:29:16.153 --> 01:29:19.628
oh, well, now I know
what's inside of a Dyson.

01:29:19.628 --> 01:29:21.144
- That's something you'd
see for a YouTube channel.

01:29:21.144 --> 01:29:22.805
- Yeah, right.

01:29:22.805 --> 01:29:23.849
What's inside of a Dyson?

01:29:23.849 --> 01:29:24.708
- What's inside of a Dyson?

01:29:24.708 --> 01:29:27.895
What if I cut this Dyson in perfect half?

01:29:27.895 --> 01:29:30.994
- I just wanna know how they did it.

01:29:30.994 --> 01:29:32.676
It's either someone has a laser cutter

01:29:32.676 --> 01:29:33.509
inside of their house,

01:29:33.509 --> 01:29:35.402
or they just went ham with a saw.

01:29:35.402 --> 01:29:36.315
I don't know what it was.

01:29:36.315 --> 01:29:37.993
- Either they have a saw in their house,

01:29:37.993 --> 01:29:38.936
or it's somewhere else,

01:29:38.936 --> 01:29:40.294
and then they brought half a Dyson

01:29:40.294 --> 01:29:42.262
to your apartment building.

01:29:42.262 --> 01:29:44.808
And then they decided that they
are done with half a Dyson,

01:29:44.808 --> 01:29:46.336
and they're gonna throw it away.

01:29:46.336 --> 01:29:47.756
- It was the weirdest thing I'd ever seen.

01:29:47.756 --> 01:29:49.683
- It's so annoying having to
get rid of big stuff in Japan.

01:29:49.683 --> 01:29:50.516
- It is.

01:29:50.516 --> 01:29:51.729
- You buy those stupid
stickers from the company.

01:29:51.729 --> 01:29:54.970
And then, you can't throw
out, if it's bigger than,

01:29:54.970 --> 01:29:56.749
I think, 30 centimeters in my apartment.

01:29:56.749 --> 01:29:58.885
- Yeah, something like that.
- Which is nothing.

01:29:58.885 --> 01:30:01.817
There's so many things that
are 30 centimeters or bigger.

01:30:01.817 --> 01:30:03.468
And if you wanna throw it
away, you have to book.

01:30:03.468 --> 01:30:05.692
And it's normally like three
weeks away if you're lucky.

01:30:05.692 --> 01:30:07.330
- Yeah, usually, it's like a month.

01:30:07.330 --> 01:30:08.740
- Now I've figured out a genius strat,

01:30:08.740 --> 01:30:12.599
which is just break the thing
down to below 30 centimeters.

01:30:12.599 --> 01:30:13.539
- [Joey] Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:30:13.539 --> 01:30:15.916
- And then you're good.

01:30:15.916 --> 01:30:17.816
You know how, in prison movies,

01:30:17.816 --> 01:30:19.177
when they escape from prison,

01:30:19.177 --> 01:30:22.016
that they start dumping
the soil one by one

01:30:22.016 --> 01:30:23.836
in the courtyard or something?

01:30:23.836 --> 01:30:26.652
It's like, all right, you
gotta break this cabinet

01:30:26.652 --> 01:30:31.434
into small pieces and slowly
recycle it every week.

01:30:31.434 --> 01:30:33.605
- I saw that the other day actually.

01:30:33.605 --> 01:30:35.165
- People do it, because they
don't wanna deal with...

01:30:35.165 --> 01:30:36.825
'Cause this shit is so annoying.

01:30:36.825 --> 01:30:39.303
- Someone had disposed of an office chair

01:30:39.303 --> 01:30:40.886
one part at a time.

01:30:42.558 --> 01:30:43.780
- I get it, I get it.

01:30:43.780 --> 01:30:46.033
- [Joey] That's so genius.

01:30:46.033 --> 01:30:48.628
- I remember seeing, I would
go take the garbage out,

01:30:48.628 --> 01:30:51.555
and one day, I saw the
bottom off, the wheels part.

01:30:51.555 --> 01:30:53.145
And I'm just like, why is
someone just getting rid

01:30:53.145 --> 01:30:54.783
of the fucking wheels part?

01:30:54.783 --> 01:30:58.574
And then, the next week, I
go to put the garbage again,

01:30:58.574 --> 01:31:00.874
and it's the seat.

01:31:00.874 --> 01:31:03.315
And then it's the seat.

01:31:03.315 --> 01:31:04.926
Someone's just playing
Jenga with office chairs.

01:31:04.926 --> 01:31:07.543
And then, next week, lo and
behold, it's the backrest.

01:31:07.543 --> 01:31:08.794
- It's slow, but it's effective.

01:31:08.794 --> 01:31:11.632
- This is the exact
reason why I bought a saw.

01:31:11.632 --> 01:31:12.465
I am not kidding.

01:31:12.465 --> 01:31:14.347
I bought a saw just to saw shit in half,

01:31:14.347 --> 01:31:15.462
so I don't have to deal with this.

01:31:15.462 --> 01:31:17.011
- I had a lot of wooden
shit, and I'm just like,

01:31:17.011 --> 01:31:18.985
I'm not paying to get rid of
this fucking wooden plank.

01:31:18.985 --> 01:31:20.661
I'm just gonna saw this bitch in half.

01:31:20.661 --> 01:31:24.400
- It's also annoying, 'cause
you have to measure it exactly.

01:31:24.400 --> 01:31:26.807
If it's even a little bit
off, they won't take it.

01:31:26.807 --> 01:31:28.470
And then you gotta wait
another three weeks

01:31:28.470 --> 01:31:30.877
and buy those stupid sticker things again.

01:31:30.877 --> 01:31:31.710
I don't wanna do this.

01:31:31.710 --> 01:31:33.841
- I had a metallic coat hanger,

01:31:33.841 --> 01:31:35.881
or a coat rack kind of thing.

01:31:35.881 --> 01:31:37.645
And of course, it was way too big,

01:31:37.645 --> 01:31:39.091
even if I took the parts off.

01:31:39.091 --> 01:31:40.394
So what did I do?

01:31:40.394 --> 01:31:42.864
I put it back up, I put it on my balcony,

01:31:42.864 --> 01:31:45.772
and just let the weather wear
it down as much as possible,

01:31:45.772 --> 01:31:47.819
to the point where I could
just snap it in half.

01:31:47.819 --> 01:31:49.800
- You let it rust?

01:31:49.800 --> 01:31:51.338
- I just let it rust to shit.

01:31:51.338 --> 01:31:54.179
And then I grab the saw or
just snap it half to the sides.

01:31:54.179 --> 01:31:55.166
I'm like, perfect.

01:31:55.166 --> 01:31:56.271
- Just let nature take its course.

01:31:56.271 --> 01:31:57.731
(Joey laughs)

01:31:57.731 --> 01:31:59.322
Erosion.

01:31:59.322 --> 01:32:00.373
- Three months later, I was like,

01:32:00.373 --> 01:32:01.232
all right, I can finally take this out.

01:32:01.232 --> 01:32:03.022
- It's the worst way to recycle something,

01:32:03.022 --> 01:32:06.460
but I respect the effort you'd go

01:32:06.460 --> 01:32:08.372
to not deal with the bureaucracy.

01:32:08.372 --> 01:32:10.218
- Yeah, dude, it probably
would've taken just as long

01:32:10.218 --> 01:32:11.550
to fucking book a time

01:32:11.550 --> 01:32:14.340
to throw this fucking coat hanger out.

01:32:14.340 --> 01:32:16.223
- Yeah, I just don't wanna
deal with it, you know?

01:32:16.223 --> 01:32:18.109
- Or I just wait for someone
to come over and be like,

01:32:18.109 --> 01:32:19.508
"Do you want this shitty
thing I don't need?

01:32:19.508 --> 01:32:20.341
Just take it please."

01:32:20.341 --> 01:32:22.266
- Dude, they make me
feel like such a bastard

01:32:22.266 --> 01:32:24.275
for using batteries.

01:32:24.275 --> 01:32:26.589
I just wanna use some AA batteries,

01:32:26.589 --> 01:32:29.718
and they make it seem
like I was using some kind

01:32:29.718 --> 01:32:32.328
of radioactive material the
way they made me get rid of it.

01:32:32.328 --> 01:32:33.508
I'm like, what's wrong with me?

01:32:33.508 --> 01:32:35.938
- I don't think I've
ever properly gotten rid

01:32:35.938 --> 01:32:36.903
of my batteries, right?

01:32:36.903 --> 01:32:37.736
Because I'm just like,

01:32:37.736 --> 01:32:40.666
okay, I'll get rid of them
next time, another time.

01:32:40.666 --> 01:32:43.557
So I have a fucking
drawer just full of used-

01:32:43.557 --> 01:32:44.390
- [Joey] Dead batteries?

01:32:44.390 --> 01:32:45.966
- Used dead batteries
that I've not been able

01:32:45.966 --> 01:32:47.017
to get rid of, because I've always-

01:32:47.017 --> 01:32:48.517
- That is the most troll
drawer in existence.

01:32:48.517 --> 01:32:49.538
- Yeah.
- Huh?

01:32:49.538 --> 01:32:50.707
- Sure, we've got a whole drawer full

01:32:50.707 --> 01:32:51.540
of batteries sitting here.

01:32:51.540 --> 01:32:52.716
Go and grab a pair.

01:32:52.716 --> 01:32:54.706
None of them are working, Garnt!

01:32:54.706 --> 01:32:56.659
- That's what you should do as a joke.

01:32:56.659 --> 01:32:59.102
Just get one actually working battery

01:32:59.102 --> 01:33:00.502
and put it in the drawer, and be like,

01:33:00.502 --> 01:33:02.743
"There is one working battery."

01:33:02.743 --> 01:33:04.153
- Find the working battery.
- Good luck.

01:33:04.153 --> 01:33:05.221
- Trash day special.

01:33:05.221 --> 01:33:06.659
- I'm gonna get rid of it someday,

01:33:06.659 --> 01:33:09.221
but I just keep forgetting the day

01:33:09.221 --> 01:33:10.346
to get rid of the batteries properly.

01:33:10.346 --> 01:33:12.929
- It's like the most fucked up "Saw" trap.

01:33:12.929 --> 01:33:16.829
There is one working
battery. You have 15 minutes.

01:33:16.829 --> 01:33:19.411
- Find the working battery.

01:33:19.411 --> 01:33:20.319
- Oh my god.

01:33:20.319 --> 01:33:21.321
- I don't really use a lot of batteries,

01:33:21.321 --> 01:33:24.833
but for a lot of the
filming stuff that we have-

01:33:24.833 --> 01:33:26.272
- Yeah, it's basically
all for the filming stuff.

01:33:26.272 --> 01:33:29.320
- It's all for mics, camera accessories.

01:33:29.320 --> 01:33:30.153
It's all batteries.

01:33:30.153 --> 01:33:32.261
It's really annoying 'cause you have

01:33:32.261 --> 01:33:33.929
to get batteries for
that, and it kinda sucks.

01:33:33.929 --> 01:33:34.809
It's like, get rechargeable ones.

01:33:34.809 --> 01:33:36.710
It's like, yeah, but I
always forget to recharge.

01:33:36.710 --> 01:33:38.182
- Yeah, but then if you
get rechargeable ones,

01:33:38.182 --> 01:33:40.869
you forget to recharge
them before the shoots,

01:33:40.869 --> 01:33:41.702
which is unfortunate.

01:33:41.702 --> 01:33:43.145
- And luckily, you can buy AAA batteries

01:33:43.145 --> 01:33:44.744
everywhere in Japan.

01:33:44.744 --> 01:33:45.864
It's pretty good for that.

01:33:45.864 --> 01:33:47.068
It's pretty good.

01:33:47.068 --> 01:33:48.696
Always done well.

01:33:48.696 --> 01:33:50.696
- Anything else you guys
been up to this week?

01:33:50.696 --> 01:33:51.796
- I'm just trying to think.

01:33:51.796 --> 01:33:53.130
- I've watched anime.

01:33:53.130 --> 01:33:54.553
I finished "Odd Taxi."

01:33:54.553 --> 01:33:56.783
- Oh, you finished "Odd Taxi?"

01:33:56.783 --> 01:33:57.674
That's surprising.

01:33:57.674 --> 01:33:59.342
Did you watch it in subbed or dubbed?

01:33:59.342 --> 01:34:00.743
- Subbed, it was good, I liked it.

01:34:00.743 --> 01:34:01.675
- Oh, nice.
- Yeah?

01:34:01.675 --> 01:34:02.822
- A very fun show.

01:34:02.822 --> 01:34:04.822
I don't know how they're
gonna make a movie.

01:34:04.822 --> 01:34:06.122
- [Joey] Oh, yeah, they are
making a movie, aren't they?

01:34:06.122 --> 01:34:08.683
- Yeah, I was surprised
when they announced

01:34:08.683 --> 01:34:10.042
that they were making a movie,

01:34:10.042 --> 01:34:13.482
just because it felt like it
just wrapped everything up.

01:34:13.482 --> 01:34:15.170
- I was like, we're done, aren't we?

01:34:15.170 --> 01:34:17.164
- Also it weirdly seemed like,

01:34:17.164 --> 01:34:20.116
I didn't think it was as
popular on the surface-

01:34:20.116 --> 01:34:21.326
- Did you watch it?
- As it made it out to be.

01:34:21.326 --> 01:34:22.173
I watched it, yeah.

01:34:22.173 --> 01:34:23.006
- Did you finish it?

01:34:23.006 --> 01:34:24.513
- Yeah, yeah.

01:34:24.513 --> 01:34:25.494
- How have we never talked about this?

01:34:25.494 --> 01:34:26.834
- I don't know.

01:34:26.834 --> 01:34:29.410
I thought I told you I finished it.

01:34:29.410 --> 01:34:30.511
- No, you didn't.

01:34:30.511 --> 01:34:31.344
I would remember.

01:34:31.344 --> 01:34:33.017
- It's because it's so rare.

01:34:33.017 --> 01:34:34.633
- I would remember if you told me

01:34:34.633 --> 01:34:36.512
you finished an anime, Joey.

01:34:36.512 --> 01:34:37.553
What the fuck?

01:34:37.553 --> 01:34:38.514
- I liked it. I thought it was good.

01:34:38.514 --> 01:34:39.874
- Yeah, I liked it. It was good.

01:34:39.874 --> 01:34:41.493
But yeah, again, I was surprised,

01:34:41.493 --> 01:34:43.686
not only because, yeah, as you said,

01:34:43.686 --> 01:34:45.784
the show wrapped up
nicely where it was like,

01:34:45.784 --> 01:34:47.132
how are they gonna make a movie out of it?

01:34:47.132 --> 01:34:48.356
But also, it's like, I don't know,

01:34:48.356 --> 01:34:49.695
I feel "Odd Taxi" was one of those shows

01:34:49.695 --> 01:34:53.612
where it got really
popular from word of mouth.

01:34:54.955 --> 01:34:57.064
I was like, did it really get that popular

01:34:57.064 --> 01:34:58.614
to warrant a movie?

01:34:58.614 --> 01:34:59.996
- I don't know how popular it got,

01:34:59.996 --> 01:35:02.317
because I remember when
I made my video on it,

01:35:02.317 --> 01:35:06.333
I made it 'cause no one was
talking about it at all.

01:35:06.333 --> 01:35:07.703
- I thought it was kinda the underdog.

01:35:07.703 --> 01:35:09.924
- Everyone who watches it I know likes it.

01:35:09.924 --> 01:35:10.991
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
- It's a great show.

01:35:10.991 --> 01:35:11.843
- But that's the thing.

01:35:11.843 --> 01:35:14.483
It's one of those shows where
I feel you start watching it,

01:35:14.483 --> 01:35:16.990
because someone who gave it a go was like,

01:35:16.990 --> 01:35:17.993
"It was really fucking good."

01:35:17.993 --> 01:35:21.946
- Yeah, I feel like it had a
similar arc to "Made in Abyss,"

01:35:21.946 --> 01:35:23.890
because when "Made in Abyss" came out,

01:35:23.890 --> 01:35:25.672
no one was watching
"Made in Abyss" at all,

01:35:25.672 --> 01:35:27.422
'cause everyone saw the art style,

01:35:27.422 --> 01:35:28.903
and everyone was just like,
oh, this is a children's show.

01:35:28.903 --> 01:35:30.159
- Children's show.

01:35:30.159 --> 01:35:32.220
- Children's show, which
couldn't be more further

01:35:32.220 --> 01:35:34.919
from the truth honestly.

01:35:34.919 --> 01:35:36.980
- There's a lot of children in the show.

01:35:36.980 --> 01:35:38.472
- I mean, yeah, it is a children's show

01:35:38.472 --> 01:35:39.789
in some sense of the word.

01:35:39.789 --> 01:35:41.652
- That's one for the kids.

01:35:41.652 --> 01:35:42.671
- One for the whole family.

01:35:42.671 --> 01:35:43.751
- They can relate. The
children can relate.

01:35:43.751 --> 01:35:44.979
- The children can relate.

01:35:44.979 --> 01:35:47.146
- The children can relate.

01:35:49.190 --> 01:35:52.328
But yeah, I mean, that was another show

01:35:52.328 --> 01:35:54.409
that really spread through word of mouth,

01:35:54.409 --> 01:35:57.071
and then eventually it
won Anime of the Year

01:35:57.071 --> 01:35:58.968
the year it came out as well.

01:35:58.968 --> 01:36:00.818
"Odd Taxi," I feel, had a similar thing

01:36:00.818 --> 01:36:03.830
where it didn't really have much promotion

01:36:03.830 --> 01:36:04.663
or anything like that,

01:36:04.663 --> 01:36:08.010
at least not that I could
see outside of Japan.

01:36:08.010 --> 01:36:12.416
In Japan, it actually had
some kind of decent promotion.

01:36:12.416 --> 01:36:13.577
I remember, when it was airing,

01:36:13.577 --> 01:36:15.557
every time you'd go in a taxi,

01:36:15.557 --> 01:36:18.279
they would have an "Odd
Taxi" advertisement.

01:36:18.279 --> 01:36:19.112
- Did they really?

01:36:19.112 --> 01:36:20.055
- Yeah, yeah, did you not see?

01:36:20.055 --> 01:36:21.331
- No, I don't remember that.
- No, I didn't see.

01:36:21.331 --> 01:36:23.248
- They'd always have it playing

01:36:23.248 --> 01:36:26.667
in the little TVs that they
have on the back of the taxis.

01:36:26.667 --> 01:36:27.808
- Did they?

01:36:27.808 --> 01:36:28.649
- At least I did.

01:36:28.649 --> 01:36:29.648
I saw a bunch of 'em.

01:36:29.648 --> 01:36:32.932
- I didn't go in enough taxis to know.

01:36:32.932 --> 01:36:34.445
- Did I talk about "Tokyo Revengers?"

01:36:34.445 --> 01:36:35.423
I watched that.

01:36:35.423 --> 01:36:36.256
- I think you-

01:36:36.256 --> 01:36:37.268
- You have not talked
about "Tokyo Revengers."

01:36:37.268 --> 01:36:38.101
- Have we not?

01:36:38.101 --> 01:36:38.934
- Have we not?

01:36:38.934 --> 01:36:40.428
- Maybe not on episode.

01:36:40.428 --> 01:36:41.963
