01:46:08.651 --> 01:46:11.214
- There's this fight that
goes on for fucking nine

01:46:11.214 --> 01:46:13.266
or eight episodes at the end.

01:46:13.266 --> 01:46:16.271
And it is the dumbest fight
I've ever seen in my life.

01:46:16.271 --> 01:46:19.688
- That sounds like some Aizen shit, dude.

01:46:20.927 --> 01:46:23.994
- It is literally the fight
of wait, there's more.

01:46:23.994 --> 01:46:26.513
Something happens, wait, there's more.

01:46:26.513 --> 01:46:27.346
Wait, there's more.

01:46:27.346 --> 01:46:29.475
And it's like, this is stupid.

01:46:29.475 --> 01:46:31.045
Just fucking resolve it.

01:46:31.045 --> 01:46:32.064
This is ridiculous.

01:46:32.064 --> 01:46:33.523
This isn't "Dragon Ball."

01:46:33.523 --> 01:46:34.663
- It's like every "Dragon Ball" fight.

01:46:34.663 --> 01:46:36.686
- This story has been somewhat concise.

01:46:36.686 --> 01:46:38.846
Yeah, they drag on a
little bit here and there.

01:46:38.846 --> 01:46:40.564
They have had some long fights,

01:46:40.564 --> 01:46:43.712
but never more than four
or five episodes, I think.

01:46:43.712 --> 01:46:45.582
It just felt like this
last fight in particular

01:46:45.582 --> 01:46:47.904
just took the absolute piss

01:46:47.904 --> 01:46:50.239
to the point where I was
like, this is just stupid.

01:46:50.239 --> 01:46:53.129
And yeah, it had a good cliffhanger.

01:46:53.129 --> 01:46:55.080
I was so bored for four episodes.

01:46:55.080 --> 01:46:56.006
- But it doesn't matter, man.

01:46:56.006 --> 01:46:57.968
All the characters are hot as fuck.

01:46:57.968 --> 01:46:59.080
According to the fan base,
according to the fan base.

01:46:59.080 --> 01:47:00.693
- They've got these characters.

01:47:00.693 --> 01:47:03.951
Yeah, I like some of the
characters in the show.

01:47:03.951 --> 01:47:07.969
My god, are so many of them insufferable.

01:47:07.969 --> 01:47:09.074
God, I mean, I liked the show.

01:47:09.074 --> 01:47:10.000
I thought it was good.

01:47:10.000 --> 01:47:13.333
Fuck, man, I felt like it blew its load,

01:47:14.599 --> 01:47:15.710
and it was making excuses.
- Is it even over?

01:47:15.710 --> 01:47:16.543
Is it even over?

01:47:16.543 --> 01:47:17.376
- No, no, it's not.
- It's not over, is it?

01:47:17.376 --> 01:47:18.532
- It's not, it's not.

01:47:18.532 --> 01:47:20.311
And I feel like where they
left it was pretty good,

01:47:20.311 --> 01:47:22.641
and it might pick up.

01:47:22.641 --> 01:47:24.938
It just felt like every single
time something happened,

01:47:24.938 --> 01:47:26.791
it was like, oh my god, there's more.

01:47:26.791 --> 01:47:27.682
Oh my god, there's more.

01:47:27.682 --> 01:47:29.920
- I don't know, I know this
is gonna sound really unfair,

01:47:29.920 --> 01:47:31.052
and this is totally my bias,

01:47:31.052 --> 01:47:32.720
but I think I only managed to make it

01:47:32.720 --> 01:47:34.268
through the first two or three episodes,

01:47:34.268 --> 01:47:37.582
because I immediately
saw what kind of theming

01:47:37.582 --> 01:47:40.020
they were going for with the story.

01:47:40.020 --> 01:47:43.775
Just a bunch of dudes just fighting...

01:47:43.775 --> 01:47:44.608
- And it's weird as well.

01:47:44.608 --> 01:47:47.509
- Good stuff, but I hate the fact

01:47:47.509 --> 01:47:51.020
that the moment I knew
where the story was heading,

01:47:51.020 --> 01:47:53.290
in my head, I was immediately just like,

01:47:53.290 --> 01:47:57.251
I'd just rather read "Baki" to be honest.

01:47:57.251 --> 01:47:58.417
- I was kind of pissed off as well

01:47:58.417 --> 01:48:01.788
that all of these kids are 13, 14.

01:48:01.788 --> 01:48:03.913
I was like, why?

01:48:03.913 --> 01:48:05.513
Just make them 17.

01:48:05.513 --> 01:48:07.083
It would make the story so much more-

01:48:07.083 --> 01:48:08.231
- [Joey] But isn't it
weird that you felt that-

01:48:08.231 --> 01:48:10.724
- It would make so much more sense.

01:48:10.724 --> 01:48:11.557
- But here's the thing.

01:48:11.557 --> 01:48:13.731
Isn't it weird that you
felt that about that show?

01:48:13.731 --> 01:48:16.112
And yet, you see Hanayama
Kaoru who's 14 years old,

01:48:16.112 --> 01:48:17.692
and you're like, perfectly understandable,

01:48:17.692 --> 01:48:19.396
have a nice day.

01:48:19.396 --> 01:48:21.252
- For some reason, it checks out.

01:48:21.252 --> 01:48:23.772
- Yeah, right, it's so weird
how it checks out though.

01:48:23.772 --> 01:48:25.188
- I don't doubt it, right?

01:48:25.188 --> 01:48:27.073
Because "Baki" never asks me once

01:48:27.073 --> 01:48:30.322
to actually believe this
world is a real world.

01:48:30.322 --> 01:48:32.471
It just completely is like, listen, bro,

01:48:32.471 --> 01:48:34.031
this is literally like the equivalent

01:48:34.031 --> 01:48:38.111
of an internet forum debate
where, can Goku beat Saitama?

01:48:38.111 --> 01:48:39.203
That is "Baki."

01:48:39.203 --> 01:48:42.095
It never once asks you to
be invested in this world,

01:48:42.095 --> 01:48:43.735
whereas "Tokyo Revengers," for me,

01:48:43.735 --> 01:48:46.205
felt like it was trying
to get me to get invested

01:48:46.205 --> 01:48:48.915
in the gangs and the culture and stuff.

01:48:48.915 --> 01:48:52.415
But at the same time, how
are you gonna make me believe

01:48:52.415 --> 01:48:55.333
that this is how 13-year-olds
and 14-year-olds react,

01:48:55.333 --> 01:48:58.400
that they drive motorcycles,
that they do all this shit,

01:48:58.400 --> 01:49:01.456
that they're willing to
rob and kill each other.

01:49:01.456 --> 01:49:04.713
If you made these kids 18,
they can still be in school.

01:49:04.713 --> 01:49:06.594
All of this would still make sense.

01:49:06.594 --> 01:49:08.187
Just do that.

01:49:08.187 --> 01:49:09.396
Why? Why?

01:49:09.396 --> 01:49:11.335
- That's basically 90% of anime,

01:49:11.335 --> 01:49:13.792
where they don't need to be that age,

01:49:13.792 --> 01:49:16.601
'cause nobody their age
actually acts like them.

01:49:16.601 --> 01:49:17.693
- This is one where I actually felt

01:49:17.693 --> 01:49:19.153
like it was to a massive detriment

01:49:19.153 --> 01:49:21.729
that they were super young.

01:49:21.729 --> 01:49:22.615
Every single plot point in the story-

01:49:22.615 --> 01:49:24.847
- Because it just made
it unbelievable, right?

01:49:24.847 --> 01:49:27.405
- Not so unbelievable, but
it made it so to the fact

01:49:27.405 --> 01:49:29.765
that it's constantly asking you

01:49:29.765 --> 01:49:33.654
to just have this level
of disbelief, to give it,

01:49:33.654 --> 01:49:36.573
okay, I guess this is how
14-year-olds would react

01:49:36.573 --> 01:49:38.594
and respond to this situation.

01:49:38.594 --> 01:49:40.696
And it's like, just add on four years.

01:49:40.696 --> 01:49:41.764
They're still in school.

01:49:41.764 --> 01:49:42.896
This can work in college.

01:49:42.896 --> 01:49:44.315
It all still works.

01:49:44.315 --> 01:49:45.725
The universe totally works.

01:49:45.725 --> 01:49:47.867
- It can work when
you're an adult as well.

01:49:47.867 --> 01:49:50.348
- And now they can ride
motorcycles no question about it.

01:49:50.348 --> 01:49:51.847
This is in Japan.

01:49:51.847 --> 01:49:53.797
No one is breaking the law in Japan.

01:49:53.797 --> 01:49:55.812
People don't even like...

01:49:55.812 --> 01:49:58.119
The only law they break
is stealing umbrellas.

01:49:58.119 --> 01:49:59.676
That's literally it, that's all they do.

01:49:59.676 --> 01:50:00.509
They don't do nothing.

01:50:00.509 --> 01:50:01.604
That's all they do.
- Pretty much.

01:50:01.604 --> 01:50:03.074
Yeah, pretty much.

01:50:03.074 --> 01:50:05.443
- How the fuck are they gonna
get a motorcycle at 13 here?

01:50:05.443 --> 01:50:08.949
- I feel like, the last time I felt that,

01:50:08.949 --> 01:50:10.233
when I felt like the characters

01:50:10.233 --> 01:50:12.755
just weren't acting their age at all,

01:50:12.755 --> 01:50:13.925
was when I watched "Erased."

01:50:13.925 --> 01:50:14.758
- I was gonna say, I knew-

01:50:14.758 --> 01:50:15.650
- Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:50:15.650 --> 01:50:16.807
- "Erased" was just like...

01:50:16.807 --> 01:50:18.161
Man, these five-year-olds.

01:50:18.161 --> 01:50:19.323
How old were they, five, six?

01:50:19.323 --> 01:50:20.882
- They were eight.
- They were nine, I think.

01:50:20.882 --> 01:50:22.981
- They're nine-year-olds acting like-

01:50:22.981 --> 01:50:24.378
- They're like, yes, using
the forms of relativity

01:50:24.378 --> 01:50:25.923
and quantum mechanics,
we can actually predict

01:50:25.923 --> 01:50:28.301
when we will reenter into
space-time continuum.

01:50:28.301 --> 01:50:32.248
- They were more capable
than veteran detectives

01:50:32.248 --> 01:50:33.681
in the force and all this shit.

01:50:33.681 --> 01:50:35.801
And I'm just like, bruh,
these are nine-year-olds,

01:50:35.801 --> 01:50:37.517
and they're acting like fucking adults.

01:50:37.517 --> 01:50:39.393
- That's why I just
couldn't get into "Erased."

01:50:39.393 --> 01:50:40.851
It's the exact same thing where I'm like,

01:50:40.851 --> 01:50:44.691
this nine-year-old girl
is solving mysteries

01:50:44.691 --> 01:50:49.166
that fucking 30-year veterans
couldn't fucking crack.

01:50:49.166 --> 01:50:52.566
- I know we've ranted about
this before and stuff.

01:50:52.566 --> 01:50:54.245
We've talked all about the age and stuff.

01:50:54.245 --> 01:50:56.805
I do understand that, a lot
of shows, I don't give a fuck.

01:50:56.805 --> 01:50:57.638
It's totally fine.

01:50:57.638 --> 01:50:58.515
- It's fiction, it's whatever.

01:50:58.515 --> 01:50:59.532
- It doesn't matter.

01:50:59.532 --> 01:51:01.673
But again, there are
some shows like "Erased"

01:51:01.673 --> 01:51:04.555
where I feel like doing
this is just completely

01:51:04.555 --> 01:51:06.453
to the detriment of the show.

01:51:06.453 --> 01:51:10.695
And it makes you suspend
belief beyond reasonable doubt.

01:51:10.695 --> 01:51:12.640
I don't know, and this
was one of the shows

01:51:12.640 --> 01:51:13.986
where I'm like, this is just stupid.

01:51:13.986 --> 01:51:16.381
- I mean, there's also
"Your Lie in April" as well,

01:51:16.381 --> 01:51:19.065
where a big thing that
took me out of the show

01:51:19.065 --> 01:51:21.604
is I feel like they were in
middle school or something.

01:51:21.604 --> 01:51:24.304
I think they're 14, 15.

01:51:24.304 --> 01:51:27.221
Everyone talks like a fucking poet.

01:51:30.233 --> 01:51:31.955
- The writing needs to match the age.

01:51:31.955 --> 01:51:33.447
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
- Yeah, yeah.

01:51:33.447 --> 01:51:35.270
- I don't give a shit if
you put 'em in the school.

01:51:35.270 --> 01:51:38.087
You've gotta write
13-year-olds like 13-year-olds.

01:51:38.087 --> 01:51:41.198
- Kosei was talking like
fucking Mozart was back then.

01:51:41.198 --> 01:51:43.238
It's like, dude, you're 15.

01:51:43.238 --> 01:51:46.684
When I was 15, all I was
thinking about poo-poo, pee-pee.

01:51:46.684 --> 01:51:47.837
- That's all I think about now. I'm 25.

01:51:47.837 --> 01:51:50.596
- That's all I think about now.

01:51:50.596 --> 01:51:52.707
You are way more sophisticated

01:51:52.707 --> 01:51:53.847
than you should be for a 15-year-old.

01:51:53.847 --> 01:51:56.975
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, this
guy came out the womb

01:51:56.975 --> 01:51:59.286
speaking in sonnets and all this shit.

01:51:59.286 --> 01:52:02.795
He was studying Shakespeare
by the age of three.

01:52:02.795 --> 01:52:05.545
My god, that took me out so much.

01:52:06.437 --> 01:52:08.088
It was a small thing,
but it was just like,

01:52:08.088 --> 01:52:10.974
you could've easily made
them at a higher age

01:52:10.974 --> 01:52:14.076
to make them feel like
they had the ability

01:52:14.076 --> 01:52:15.926
to speak like this.

01:52:15.926 --> 01:52:17.705
They were 14 years old.

01:52:17.705 --> 01:52:19.822
That was the biggest thing that worried.

01:52:19.822 --> 01:52:20.655
- It's annoying.

01:52:20.655 --> 01:52:22.452
Sometimes, it's shows where they write

01:52:22.452 --> 01:52:23.798
the characters like 17-year-olds.

01:52:23.798 --> 01:52:26.179
They act and talk like 17-year-olds.

01:52:26.179 --> 01:52:27.948
They behave like 17-year-olds.

01:52:27.948 --> 01:52:30.758
Why not just make them
fucking 17-year-olds?

01:52:30.758 --> 01:52:32.261
- That's why I think, to this day,

01:52:32.261 --> 01:52:36.011
the most perfect example
of a perfectly aged,

01:52:37.860 --> 01:52:39.301
a character's acting age appropriate

01:52:39.301 --> 01:52:42.052
in a super realistic
way, was "Golden Time."

01:52:42.052 --> 01:52:44.232
Because it was like, they were in college,

01:52:44.232 --> 01:52:46.043
and yet they were super immature

01:52:46.043 --> 01:52:48.443
like most college students are.

01:52:48.443 --> 01:52:50.581
That's a realistic character.
- I like that show.

01:52:50.581 --> 01:52:51.620
- I love "Golden Time."

01:52:51.620 --> 01:52:53.440
- Yeah, and that's why
that show was so good,

01:52:53.440 --> 01:52:55.489
and it was so immersive,
because it's like,

01:52:55.489 --> 01:52:58.334
yeah, I know people who
are like this in college.

01:52:58.334 --> 01:52:59.393
- You're such a breath of fresh air

01:52:59.393 --> 01:53:00.240
to have it set in college.

01:53:00.240 --> 01:53:03.569
- Yeah, but they were acting
more like high school students

01:53:03.569 --> 01:53:07.986
than most high school
students were in other shows.

01:53:07.986 --> 01:53:09.411
It's so fucking ironic.

01:53:09.411 --> 01:53:11.999
- Yeah, I feel like that's
why, to me even now,

01:53:11.999 --> 01:53:13.929
"Golden Time" is one of
my favorite romances-

01:53:13.929 --> 01:53:15.909
- I love "Golden Time."
- In all of anime.

01:53:15.909 --> 01:53:17.517
Just because it actually felt

01:53:17.517 --> 01:53:21.650
like these were believable
characters set in a world

01:53:21.650 --> 01:53:24.230
that felt like it was based in reality,

01:53:24.230 --> 01:53:27.397
not in this anime world
where 15-year-olds-

01:53:27.397 --> 01:53:29.506
- 15-year-olds are doing quantum physics.

01:53:29.506 --> 01:53:32.989
- 15-year-olds are doing quantum physics.

01:53:32.989 --> 01:53:35.697
I mean, you look at fucking
Naruto and Sasuke, they-

01:53:35.697 --> 01:53:36.530
- "Hunter x Hunter" was another one

01:53:36.530 --> 01:53:38.143
where I felt like they
got the characters' ages,

01:53:38.143 --> 01:53:40.985
it actually reflected their personality.

01:53:40.985 --> 01:53:42.402
Gon was an idiot.

01:53:44.473 --> 01:53:47.602
He would be convinced to
do stuff by strangers.

01:53:47.602 --> 01:53:48.551
- Right, right.

01:53:48.551 --> 01:53:49.717
- Like a 12-year-old-
- Like a child.

01:53:49.717 --> 01:53:51.577
- Like a 13-year-old, unfortunately.

01:53:51.577 --> 01:53:53.890
No one over the age of 18
is hanging out with Hisoka,

01:53:53.890 --> 01:53:54.723
you know what I mean?

01:53:54.723 --> 01:53:55.632
Let's be honest.

01:53:55.632 --> 01:53:56.465
- For good reason.

01:53:56.465 --> 01:53:57.428
- [All] For a good reason.

01:53:57.428 --> 01:53:58.993
- 'Cause everyone could
tell you he's a creep.

01:53:58.993 --> 01:54:00.206
But Gon is like-
- For their own protection.

01:54:00.206 --> 01:54:01.696
- Gon's like, oh, he's talking to me.

01:54:01.696 --> 01:54:03.586
Okay, I'll talk back.

01:54:03.586 --> 01:54:06.427
I appreciate it when shows actually treat

01:54:06.427 --> 01:54:08.579
the characters like their age.

01:54:08.579 --> 01:54:09.412
It pissed me off.

01:54:09.412 --> 01:54:11.618
- 'Cause a lot of people,
for example, Naruto,

01:54:11.618 --> 01:54:15.392
a lot of people forget
that, in the OG "Naruto,"-

01:54:15.392 --> 01:54:16.225
- He's 10.

01:54:16.225 --> 01:54:18.879
- They're 11 and 12 years old.

01:54:18.879 --> 01:54:20.207
You look at some of the
shit they go through.

01:54:20.207 --> 01:54:23.211
Sasuke is trying to revenge
his entire fucking clan

01:54:23.211 --> 01:54:24.960
at the age of 11.

01:54:24.960 --> 01:54:25.793
11!

01:54:27.956 --> 01:54:29.246
He's doing that, right?

01:54:29.246 --> 01:54:31.205
- This man's listened to too
much My Chemical Romance, dude.

01:54:31.205 --> 01:54:32.216
- Right, right, right.

01:54:32.216 --> 01:54:34.148
- Get off that shit,
and go to fucking hell.

01:54:34.148 --> 01:54:35.375
- I'll avenge my fucking Big Mac

01:54:35.375 --> 01:54:37.446
if someone slaps it out
of my hand when I'm 11.

01:54:37.446 --> 01:54:39.147
So I believe that actually.

01:54:39.147 --> 01:54:40.391
I was a very petty 11-year-old.

01:54:40.391 --> 01:54:42.641
- Most realistic character.

01:54:44.432 --> 01:54:45.390
- I don't know, man.

01:54:45.390 --> 01:54:48.902
I just kinda wish that it
would change a little bit.

01:54:48.902 --> 01:54:50.143
And that was one of the main reasons

01:54:50.143 --> 01:54:53.124
why I was a bit harsh
on "Tokyo Revengers."

01:54:53.124 --> 01:54:54.401
And that's why I got more annoyed with it,

01:54:54.401 --> 01:54:56.423
'cause it felt like it was just
getting stupid right there.

01:54:56.423 --> 01:54:59.813
- I don't know if I've
just seen so much anime

01:54:59.813 --> 01:55:02.646
that I'm just immune to this shit.

01:55:05.573 --> 01:55:08.923
It's very rare that a
character's age really comes

01:55:08.923 --> 01:55:11.454
into any kind of specific plot point

01:55:11.454 --> 01:55:14.725
or any bearing on the plot itself.

01:55:14.725 --> 01:55:17.415
It's so hard to tell a
character's age in anime

01:55:17.415 --> 01:55:20.393
based on just their
looks and their actions,

01:55:20.393 --> 01:55:25.393
because the range of anime
characters from 13 to fucking 28,

01:55:26.747 --> 01:55:27.982
they all look the same,

01:55:27.982 --> 01:55:30.133
and they all act the same.
- They act the same, yeah.

01:55:30.133 --> 01:55:32.815
- It's kinda like Japanese
people in real life, isn't it?

01:55:32.815 --> 01:55:33.863
- Maybe that's why!

01:55:33.863 --> 01:55:34.723
Maybe that's why!
- That's probably why.

01:55:34.723 --> 01:55:35.556
- Right, right.

01:55:35.556 --> 01:55:37.345
- They turn to adults-

01:55:37.345 --> 01:55:38.762
- You look at a Japanese girl,

01:55:38.762 --> 01:55:41.845
and you're like, you can be 12 or 30.

01:55:42.709 --> 01:55:43.861
And I'm kind of afraid to ask.

01:55:43.861 --> 01:55:46.673
- Did you see, as well,
for the "Tokyo Revengers,"

01:55:46.673 --> 01:55:49.821
they made an uncensored version?

01:55:49.821 --> 01:55:53.522
Because they used the temple symbol a lot,

01:55:53.522 --> 01:55:55.689
which is unfortunately is-

01:55:56.659 --> 01:55:57.492
- A manji?
- A swastika turned.

